-- Constitutions.

`a clean constitution` MEANS Constitution WITH
    `description` IS "no reservation of control to any public office-holder"
    `express permission for the entity's activities to be directed or otherwise controlled by a Minister` IS FALSE
    `express permission for the entity's activities to be directed or otherwise controlled by a member of the States Assembly` IS FALSE
    `express permission for the entity's activities to be directed or otherwise controlled by any equivalent of such a person in another jurisdiction` IS FALSE
    `express permission for any of the entity's governors to be a Minister` IS FALSE
    `express permission for any of the entity's governors to be a member of the States Assembly` IS FALSE
    `express permission for any of the entity's governors to be any equivalent of such a person in another jurisdiction` IS FALSE
    `that permission extended to such a person acting in that capacity` IS FALSE

`a constitution reserving Ministerial direction` MEANS Constitution WITH
    `description` IS "Article 7: the Minister may direct the activities of the trust"
    `express permission for the entity's activities to be directed or otherwise controlled by a Minister` IS TRUE
    `express permission for the entity's activities to be directed or otherwise controlled by a member of the States Assembly` IS FALSE
    `express permission for the entity's activities to be directed or otherwise controlled by any equivalent of such a person in another jurisdiction` IS FALSE
    `express permission for any of the entity's governors to be a Minister` IS FALSE
    `express permission for any of the entity's governors to be a member of the States Assembly` IS FALSE
    `express permission for any of the entity's governors to be any equivalent of such a person in another jurisdiction` IS FALSE
    `that permission extended to such a person acting in that capacity` IS TRUE

`a constitution reserving a States Assembly governorship` MEANS Constitution WITH
    `description` IS "Article 4: one seat on the council is reserved to a member of the States Assembly"
    `express permission for the entity's activities to be directed or otherwise controlled by a Minister` IS FALSE
    `express permission for the entity's activities to be directed or otherwise controlled by a member of the States Assembly` IS FALSE
    `express permission for the entity's activities to be directed or otherwise controlled by any equivalent of such a person in another jurisdiction` IS FALSE
    `express permission for any of the entity's governors to be a Minister` IS FALSE
    `express permission for any of the entity's governors to be a member of the States Assembly` IS TRUE
    `express permission for any of the entity's governors to be any equivalent of such a person in another jurisdiction` IS FALSE
    `that permission extended to such a person acting in that capacity` IS TRUE

`a constitution reserving a foreign-equivalent governorship` MEANS Constitution WITH
    `description` IS "Article 4: one seat is reserved to a member of the Guernsey States of Deliberation"
    `express permission for the entity's activities to be directed or otherwise controlled by a Minister` IS FALSE
    `express permission for the entity's activities to be directed or otherwise controlled by a member of the States Assembly` IS FALSE
    `express permission for the entity's activities to be directed or otherwise controlled by any equivalent of such a person in another jurisdiction` IS FALSE
    `express permission for any of the entity's governors to be a Minister` IS FALSE
    `express permission for any of the entity's governors to be a member of the States Assembly` IS FALSE
    `express permission for any of the entity's governors to be any equivalent of such a person in another jurisdiction` IS TRUE
    `that permission extended to such a person acting in that capacity` IS TRUE

-- The "acting in that capacity" qualifier failing: the constitution permits a
-- person who happens to hold office to serve, but in a private capacity only.
`a constitution admitting a Minister in a private capacity` MEANS Constitution WITH
    `description` IS "Article 4: a governor who is a Minister serves in a personal capacity and not ex officio"
    `express permission for the entity's activities to be directed or otherwise controlled by a Minister` IS FALSE
    `express permission for the entity's activities to be directed or otherwise controlled by a member of the States Assembly` IS FALSE
    `express permission for the entity's activities to be directed or otherwise controlled by any equivalent of such a person in another jurisdiction` IS FALSE
    `express permission for any of the entity's governors to be a Minister` IS TRUE
    `express permission for any of the entity's governors to be a member of the States Assembly` IS FALSE
    `express permission for any of the entity's governors to be any equivalent of such a person in another jurisdiction` IS FALSE
    `that permission extended to such a person acting in that capacity` IS FALSE

-- Public benefit findings.

`a sound public benefit finding` MEANS PublicBenefitFinding WITH
    `description` IS "benefit to the public at large, properly determined"
    `public benefit in Jersey or elsewhere, to a reasonable degree, provided in giving effect to those purposes` IS TRUE
    `public benefit in Jersey or elsewhere, to a reasonable degree, intended to be provided in giving effect to those purposes` IS TRUE
    `benefit provided only to one particular natural person or to a group of identified natural persons` IS FALSE
    `benefit provided to a section of the public only` IS FALSE
    `any condition on obtaining that benefit (including any charge or fee) unduly restrictive` IS FALSE
    `regard had to the comparison required by Article 7(2)(a)` IS TRUE
    `regard had to the question required by Article 7(2)(b)` IS FALSE
    `a particular charitable purpose presumed to be for the public benefit` IS FALSE

`a finding of no public benefit` MEANS PublicBenefitFinding WITH
    `description` IS "no benefit provided or intended"
    `public benefit in Jersey or elsewhere, to a reasonable degree, provided in giving effect to those purposes` IS FALSE
    `public benefit in Jersey or elsewhere, to a reasonable degree, intended to be provided in giving effect to those purposes` IS FALSE
    `benefit provided only to one particular natural person or to a group of identified natural persons` IS FALSE
    `benefit provided to a section of the public only` IS FALSE
    `any condition on obtaining that benefit (including any charge or fee) unduly restrictive` IS FALSE
    `regard had to the comparison required by Article 7(2)(a)` IS TRUE
    `regard had to the question required by Article 7(2)(b)` IS FALSE
    `a particular charitable purpose presumed to be for the public benefit` IS FALSE

`a finding of intended but not actual public benefit` MEANS PublicBenefitFinding WITH
    `description` IS "not yet operating; benefit intended"
    `public benefit in Jersey or elsewhere, to a reasonable degree, provided in giving effect to those purposes` IS FALSE
    `public benefit in Jersey or elsewhere, to a reasonable degree, intended to be provided in giving effect to those purposes` IS TRUE
    `benefit provided only to one particular natural person or to a group of identified natural persons` IS FALSE
    `benefit provided to a section of the public only` IS FALSE
    `any condition on obtaining that benefit (including any charge or fee) unduly restrictive` IS FALSE
    `regard had to the comparison required by Article 7(2)(a)` IS TRUE
    `regard had to the question required by Article 7(2)(b)` IS FALSE
    `a particular charitable purpose presumed to be for the public benefit` IS FALSE

`a finding that benefit reaches only identified individuals` MEANS PublicBenefitFinding WITH
    `description` IS "the trust benefits the settlor's four named grandchildren"
    `public benefit in Jersey or elsewhere, to a reasonable degree, provided in giving effect to those purposes` IS TRUE
    `public benefit in Jersey or elsewhere, to a reasonable degree, intended to be provided in giving effect to those purposes` IS TRUE
    `benefit provided only to one particular natural person or to a group of identified natural persons` IS TRUE
    `benefit provided to a section of the public only` IS TRUE
    `any condition on obtaining that benefit (including any charge or fee) unduly restrictive` IS FALSE
    `regard had to the comparison required by Article 7(2)(a)` IS TRUE
    `regard had to the question required by Article 7(2)(b)` IS TRUE
    `a particular charitable purpose presumed to be for the public benefit` IS FALSE

`a finding with an unduly restrictive fee` MEANS PublicBenefitFinding WITH
    `description` IS "benefit to a section of the public, behind a fee the determiner found unduly restrictive"
    `public benefit in Jersey or elsewhere, to a reasonable degree, provided in giving effect to those purposes` IS TRUE
    `public benefit in Jersey or elsewhere, to a reasonable degree, intended to be provided in giving effect to those purposes` IS TRUE
    `benefit provided only to one particular natural person or to a group of identified natural persons` IS FALSE
    `benefit provided to a section of the public only` IS TRUE
    `any condition on obtaining that benefit (including any charge or fee) unduly restrictive` IS TRUE
    `regard had to the comparison required by Article 7(2)(a)` IS TRUE
    `regard had to the question required by Article 7(2)(b)` IS TRUE
    `a particular charitable purpose presumed to be for the public benefit` IS FALSE

`a finding made on a presumption` MEANS PublicBenefitFinding WITH
    `description` IS "public benefit presumed from the advancement of religion, contrary to Article 7(3)(a)"
    `public benefit in Jersey or elsewhere, to a reasonable degree, provided in giving effect to those purposes` IS TRUE
    `public benefit in Jersey or elsewhere, to a reasonable degree, intended to be provided in giving effect to those purposes` IS TRUE
    `benefit provided only to one particular natural person or to a group of identified natural persons` IS FALSE
    `benefit provided to a section of the public only` IS FALSE
    `any condition on obtaining that benefit (including any charge or fee) unduly restrictive` IS FALSE
    `regard had to the comparison required by Article 7(2)(a)` IS TRUE
    `regard had to the question required by Article 7(2)(b)` IS FALSE
    `a particular charitable purpose presumed to be for the public benefit` IS TRUE

`a finding that skipped the section-of-the-public question` MEANS PublicBenefitFinding WITH
    `description` IS "benefit to a section of the public only, but Article 7(2)(b) was never asked"
    `public benefit in Jersey or elsewhere, to a reasonable degree, provided in giving effect to those purposes` IS TRUE
    `public benefit in Jersey or elsewhere, to a reasonable degree, intended to be provided in giving effect to those purposes` IS TRUE
    `benefit provided only to one particular natural person or to a group of identified natural persons` IS FALSE
    `benefit provided to a section of the public only` IS TRUE
    `any condition on obtaining that benefit (including any charge or fee) unduly restrictive` IS FALSE
    `regard had to the comparison required by Article 7(2)(a)` IS TRUE
    `regard had to the question required by Article 7(2)(b)` IS FALSE
    `a particular charitable purpose presumed to be for the public benefit` IS FALSE

-- Entities. A GIVEN-parameterised constructor: L4 has no record-update
-- operator, so each scenario supplies every field, varying only the operative
-- ones.
GIVEN `the name`        IS A STRING
      `the purposes`    IS A LIST OF Purpose
      `a constitution`  IS A Constitution
      `applicant`       IS A BOOLEAN
      `the finding`     IS A PublicBenefitFinding
      `an Order`        IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN Entity
`an entity` MEANS Entity WITH
    `name` IS `the name`
    `purposes` IS `the purposes`
    `constitution` IS `a constitution`
    `an applicant` IS `applicant`
    `the public benefit finding` IS `the finding`
    `specified in an Order under Article 5(3) disapplying paragraph (2)` IS `an Order`

`the St Helier poverty trust` MEANS
    `an entity` "the St Helier poverty trust" (LIST `a poverty-relief purpose`)
        `a clean constitution` FALSE `a sound public benefit finding` FALSE

`the poverty trust with a charity shop` MEANS
    `an entity` "the poverty trust with a charity shop"
        (LIST `a poverty-relief purpose`, `an ancillary fundraising purpose`)
        `a clean constitution` FALSE `a sound public benefit finding` FALSE

`the charity shop with nothing behind it` MEANS
    `an entity` "the charity shop with nothing behind it" (LIST `an ancillary fundraising purpose`)
        `a clean constitution` FALSE `a sound public benefit finding` FALSE

`the poverty trust with a party-political object` MEANS
    `an entity` "the poverty trust with a party-political object"
        (LIST `a poverty-relief purpose`, `a party-political purpose`)
        `a clean constitution` FALSE `a sound public benefit finding` FALSE

`the poverty trust with incidental campaigning` MEANS
    `an entity` "the poverty trust with incidental campaigning"
        (LIST `a poverty-relief purpose`, `an ancillary party-political purpose`)
        `a clean constitution` FALSE `a sound public benefit finding` FALSE

`the grocery company` MEANS
    `an entity` "the grocery company" (LIST `a purely commercial purpose`)
        `a clean constitution` FALSE `a sound public benefit finding` FALSE

`the entity with no purposes` MEANS
    `an entity` "the entity with no purposes" EMPTY
        `a clean constitution` FALSE `a sound public benefit finding` FALSE

`the entity with no purposes and no benefit` MEANS
    `an entity` "the entity with no purposes and no benefit" EMPTY
        `a clean constitution` FALSE `a finding of no public benefit` FALSE

`the disease-prevention trust` MEANS
    `an entity` "the disease-prevention trust" (LIST `a sickness-prevention purpose`)
        `a clean constitution` FALSE `a sound public benefit finding` FALSE

`the pigeon fanciers' association` MEANS
    `an entity` "the pigeon fanciers' association" (LIST `a spectator-pastime purpose`)
        `a clean constitution` FALSE `a sound public benefit finding` FALSE

`the island swimming association` MEANS
    `an entity` "the island swimming association" (LIST `a physical-sport purpose`)
        `a clean constitution` FALSE `a sound public benefit finding` FALSE

`the members-only tennis club` MEANS
    `an entity` "the members-only tennis club" (LIST `a members-only recreation purpose`)
        `a clean constitution` FALSE `a sound public benefit finding` FALSE

`the public recreation ground trust` MEANS
    `an entity` "the public recreation ground trust" (LIST `an open recreation purpose`)
        `a clean constitution` FALSE `a sound public benefit finding` FALSE

`the humanist society` MEANS
    `an entity` "the humanist society" (LIST `a philosophical-belief purpose`)
        `a clean constitution` FALSE `a sound public benefit finding` FALSE

`the Ministerially directed trust` MEANS
    `an entity` "the Ministerially directed trust" (LIST `a poverty-relief purpose`)
        `a constitution reserving Ministerial direction` FALSE `a sound public benefit finding` FALSE

`the Ministerially directed trust exempted by Order` MEANS
    `an entity` "the Ministerially directed trust exempted by Order" (LIST `a poverty-relief purpose`)
        `a constitution reserving Ministerial direction` FALSE `a sound public benefit finding` TRUE

`the States-governed foundation` MEANS
    `an entity` "the States-governed foundation" (LIST `a poverty-relief purpose`)
        `a constitution reserving a States Assembly governorship` FALSE `a sound public benefit finding` FALSE

`the Guernsey-governed foundation` MEANS
    `an entity` "the Guernsey-governed foundation" (LIST `a poverty-relief purpose`)
        `a constitution reserving a foreign-equivalent governorship` FALSE `a sound public benefit finding` FALSE

`the trust with a Minister in a private capacity` MEANS
    `an entity` "the trust with a Minister in a private capacity" (LIST `a poverty-relief purpose`)
        `a constitution admitting a Minister in a private capacity` FALSE `a sound public benefit finding` FALSE

`the dormant registered charity` MEANS
    `an entity` "the dormant registered charity" (LIST `a poverty-relief purpose`)
        `a clean constitution` FALSE `a finding of intended but not actual public benefit` FALSE

`the applicant not yet operating` MEANS
    `an entity` "the applicant not yet operating" (LIST `a poverty-relief purpose`)
        `a clean constitution` TRUE `a finding of intended but not actual public benefit` FALSE

`the grandchildren's trust` MEANS
    `an entity` "the grandchildren's trust" (LIST `a poverty-relief purpose`)
        `a clean constitution` FALSE `a finding that benefit reaches only identified individuals` FALSE

`the school with an unduly restrictive fee` MEANS
    `an entity` "the school with an unduly restrictive fee" (LIST `a poverty-relief purpose`)
        `a clean constitution` FALSE `a finding with an unduly restrictive fee` FALSE

`the church whose benefit was presumed` MEANS
    `an entity` "the church whose benefit was presumed" (LIST `a poverty-relief purpose`)
        `a clean constitution` FALSE `a finding made on a presumption` FALSE

`the entity whose determiner skipped 7(2)(b)` MEANS
    `an entity` "the entity whose determiner skipped 7(2)(b)" (LIST `a poverty-relief purpose`)
        `a clean constitution` FALSE `a finding that skipped the section-of-the-public question` FALSE

§§ `Assertions`

§§§ `Article 6(1) — each head, positive and negative`

#ASSERT     `(a) — the prevention or relief of poverty` `a poverty-relief purpose`
#ASSERT NOT `(a) — the prevention or relief of poverty` `a purely commercial purpose`
#ASSERT NOT `(b) — the advancement of education` `a poverty-relief purpose`
#ASSERT NOT `(c) — the advancement of religion` `a philosophical-belief purpose`
#ASSERT NOT `(e) — the saving of lives` `a poverty-relief purpose`
#ASSERT NOT `(g) — the advancement of the arts, heritage, culture or science` `a poverty-relief purpose`
#ASSERT NOT `(j) — the advancement of human rights, conflict resolution or reconciliation` `a poverty-relief purpose`
#ASSERT NOT `(k) — the promotion of religious or racial harmony` `a poverty-relief purpose`
#ASSERT     `(l) — the promotion of equality and diversity` `a party-political purpose`
#ASSERT NOT `(l) — the promotion of equality and diversity` `a poverty-relief purpose`
#ASSERT NOT `(m) — the advancement of environmental protection or improvement` `a poverty-relief purpose`
#ASSERT NOT `(n) — the relief of those in need` `a poverty-relief purpose`
#ASSERT NOT `(o) — the advancement of animal welfare` `a poverty-relief purpose`

§§§ `Article 6(2)(a) — the health widening`

-- The disease-prevention trust does NOT claim to advance health; it reaches
-- head (d) only because 6(2)(a) widens the head to reach it.
#ASSERT     `(d) — the advancement of health` `a sickness-prevention purpose`
#ASSERT NOT `(d) — the advancement of health` `a poverty-relief purpose`

§§§ `Article 6(2)(c) — the sport gate, exercised both ways`

#ASSERT NOT `(h) — the advancement of public participation in sport` `a spectator-pastime purpose`
#ASSERT     `(h) — the advancement of public participation in sport` `a physical-sport purpose`
-- The gate is what separates them: both claim the head, one satisfies 6(2)(c).
#ASSERT `a spectator-pastime purpose`'s `the advancement of public participation in sport`
#ASSERT `a physical-sport purpose`'s   `the advancement of public participation in sport`

§§§ `Article 6(2)(d) — the recreational-facilities gate, exercised both ways`

#ASSERT NOT `(2)(d) — the recreational-facilities restriction is satisfied` `a members-only recreation purpose`
#ASSERT     `(2)(d) — the recreational-facilities restriction is satisfied` `an open recreation purpose`
#ASSERT NOT `(i) — the provision of recreational facilities or activities` `a members-only recreation purpose`
#ASSERT     `(i) — the provision of recreational facilities or activities` `an open recreation purpose`

§§§ `Article 6(2)(f) — the philosophical-belief deeming into head (p)`

-- No separate analogy judgement was made; the purpose reaches (p) by 6(2)(f).
#ASSERT NOT `a philosophical-belief purpose`'s `reasonably regarded as analogous to any of the purposes listed in sub-paragraphs (a) to (o)`
#ASSERT     `(p) — any other analogous purpose` `a philosophical-belief purpose`
#ASSERT NOT `(p) — any other analogous purpose` `a poverty-relief purpose`

§§§ `Article 6(5) — the political-purposes carve-out, exercised both ways`

#ASSERT     `(5) — the purpose is excluded as political` `a party-political purpose`
#ASSERT NOT `(5) — the purpose is excluded as political` `a poverty-relief purpose`
-- A political purpose that WOULD otherwise fall within paragraph (1) still
-- does; 6(5) removes it at the charitable-purpose step, not at the head.
#ASSERT     `the purpose falls within paragraph (1)` `a party-political purpose`
#ASSERT NOT `the purpose is a charitable purpose`   `a party-political purpose`
#ASSERT     `the purpose is a charitable purpose`   `a poverty-relief purpose`
#ASSERT NOT `the purpose is a charitable purpose`   `a purely commercial purpose`
#ASSERT NOT `the purpose is a charitable purpose`   `an ancillary fundraising purpose`

§§§ `Article 5(1)(a)(ii) — the ancillary limb, and its referential gate (A9)`

#ASSERT     `(ii) — the purpose is purely ancillary or incidental` `the poverty trust with a charity shop` `an ancillary fundraising purpose`
-- Same purpose, entity with no charitable purpose to be ancillary TO: fails.
#ASSERT NOT `(ii) — the purpose is purely ancillary or incidental` `the charity shop with nothing behind it` `an ancillary fundraising purpose`
-- 6(5)'s second half: a political purpose cannot be rescued by calling it
-- ancillary, even inside an entity that has a charitable purpose.
#ASSERT NOT `(ii) — the purpose is purely ancillary or incidental` `the poverty trust with incidental campaigning` `an ancillary party-political purpose`
#ASSERT     `an ancillary party-political purpose`'s `purely ancillary or incidental to any of the entity's charitable purposes`

§§§ `Article 5(1)(a) — all of its purposes`

#ASSERT     `5(1)(a) — all of its purposes are charitable or ancillary` `the St Helier poverty trust`
#ASSERT     `5(1)(a) — all of its purposes are charitable or ancillary` `the poverty trust with a charity shop`
#ASSERT NOT `5(1)(a) — all of its purposes are charitable or ancillary` `the charity shop with nothing behind it`
#ASSERT NOT `5(1)(a) — all of its purposes are charitable or ancillary` `the poverty trust with a party-political object`
#ASSERT NOT `5(1)(a) — all of its purposes are charitable or ancillary` `the poverty trust with incidental campaigning`
#ASSERT NOT `5(1)(a) — all of its purposes are charitable or ancillary` `the grocery company`
-- AMBIGUITY A10 pinned: vacuous truth over the empty purpose list.
#ASSERT     `5(1)(a) — all of its purposes are charitable or ancillary` `the entity with no purposes`

§§§ `Article 5(1)(b) and Article 7 — public benefit`

#ASSERT     `5(1)(b) — public benefit` `the St Helier poverty trust`
#ASSERT NOT `5(1)(b) — public benefit` `the entity with no purposes and no benefit`
-- AMBIGUITY A11 exercised both ways: intention avails an applicant only.
#ASSERT     `the applicant's intention limb` `the applicant not yet operating`
#ASSERT NOT `the applicant's intention limb` `the dormant registered charity`
#ASSERT     `5(1)(b) — public benefit` `the applicant not yet operating`
#ASSERT NOT `5(1)(b) — public benefit` `the dormant registered charity`
-- AMBIGUITY A6: 7(3)(b) is a hard bar and overrides an affirmative finding.
#ASSERT     `the grandchildren's trust`'s `the public benefit finding`'s `public benefit in Jersey or elsewhere, to a reasonable degree, provided in giving effect to those purposes`
#ASSERT     `7(3)(b) — the entity benefits only identified natural persons` `the grandchildren's trust`
#ASSERT NOT `5(1)(b) — public benefit` `the grandchildren's trust`
#ASSERT NOT `7(3)(b) — the entity benefits only identified natural persons` `the St Helier poverty trust`
-- AMBIGUITY A7: an unduly restrictive condition is a consideration, not a
-- defeater. The finding records it; the truth value is unmoved.
#ASSERT     `the school with an unduly restrictive fee`'s `the public benefit finding`'s `any condition on obtaining that benefit (including any charge or fee) unduly restrictive`
#ASSERT     `5(1)(b) — public benefit` `the school with an unduly restrictive fee`

§§§ `Article 7(2) and 7(3)(a) — the determination's own validity (A8)`

#ASSERT     `the public benefit determination was properly made` `the St Helier poverty trust`
-- 7(2)(b)'s duty is vacuously discharged when benefit is not confined to a
-- section of the public, even though the question was not asked.
#ASSERT NOT `the St Helier poverty trust`'s `the public benefit finding`'s `regard had to the question required by Article 7(2)(b)`
#ASSERT     `7(2)(b) — the section-of-the-public question was reached` `the St Helier poverty trust`
-- ... and bites when it is.
#ASSERT NOT `7(2)(b) — the section-of-the-public question was reached` `the entity whose determiner skipped 7(2)(b)`
#ASSERT NOT `the public benefit determination was properly made` `the entity whose determiner skipped 7(2)(b)`
#ASSERT     `7(2)(b) — the section-of-the-public question was reached` `the school with an unduly restrictive fee`
-- 7(3)(a): a presumption invalidates the determination ...
#ASSERT NOT `7(3)(a) — no charitable purpose was presumed to be for the public benefit` `the church whose benefit was presumed`
#ASSERT NOT `the public benefit determination was properly made` `the church whose benefit was presumed`
-- ... but under A8 does NOT change the entity's status on the merits.
#ASSERT     `the entity meets the charity test` `the church whose benefit was presumed`

§§§ `Article 5(2) and 5(3) — the government-control carve-out, exercised both ways`

-- A12 reading (i): the tabulated list serves BOTH modes. Direction mode ...
#ASSERT     `5(2) — direction or control by a listed person is expressly permitted` `the Ministerially directed trust`
#ASSERT NOT `5(2) — governorship by a listed person is expressly permitted` `the Ministerially directed trust`
#ASSERT     `5(2) — the government-control disqualification applies` `the Ministerially directed trust`
-- ... and governor mode, limbs (b) and (c).
#ASSERT NOT `5(2) — direction or control by a listed person is expressly permitted` `the States-governed foundation`
#ASSERT     `5(2) — governorship by a listed person is expressly permitted` `the States-governed foundation`
#ASSERT     `5(2) — the government-control disqualification applies` `the States-governed foundation`
#ASSERT     `5(2) — governorship by a listed person is expressly permitted` `the Guernsey-governed foundation`
#ASSERT     `5(2) — the government-control disqualification applies` `the Guernsey-governed foundation`
-- Clean constitution: neither mode.
#ASSERT NOT `5(2) — a listed person is expressly permitted under either mode` `the St Helier poverty trust`
#ASSERT NOT `5(2) — the government-control disqualification applies` `the St Helier poverty trust`
-- The "acting in that capacity" qualifier, exercised negatively: the permission
-- exists but is confined to a private capacity.
#ASSERT     `5(2) — governorship by a listed person is expressly permitted` `the trust with a Minister in a private capacity`
#ASSERT NOT `5(2) — the government-control disqualification applies` `the trust with a Minister in a private capacity`
-- 5(3): an Order disapplies paragraph (2) for an otherwise-caught entity.
#ASSERT     `5(2) — a listed person is expressly permitted under either mode` `the Ministerially directed trust exempted by Order`
#ASSERT NOT `5(2) — the government-control disqualification applies` `the Ministerially directed trust exempted by Order`

§§§ `Article 5 — the charity test end to end`

#ASSERT     `the entity meets the charity test` `the St Helier poverty trust`
#ASSERT     `the entity meets the charity test` `the poverty trust with a charity shop`
#ASSERT     `the entity meets the charity test` `the disease-prevention trust`
#ASSERT     `the entity meets the charity test` `the island swimming association`
#ASSERT     `the entity meets the charity test` `the public recreation ground trust`
#ASSERT     `the entity meets the charity test` `the humanist society`
#ASSERT     `the entity meets the charity test` `the applicant not yet operating`
#ASSERT     `the entity meets the charity test` `the school with an unduly restrictive fee`
#ASSERT     `the entity meets the charity test` `the Ministerially directed trust exempted by Order`
#ASSERT     `the entity meets the charity test` `the trust with a Minister in a private capacity`

#ASSERT NOT `the entity meets the charity test` `the charity shop with nothing behind it`
#ASSERT NOT `the entity meets the charity test` `the poverty trust with a party-political object`
#ASSERT NOT `the entity meets the charity test` `the poverty trust with incidental campaigning`
#ASSERT NOT `the entity meets the charity test` `the grocery company`
#ASSERT NOT `the entity meets the charity test` `the pigeon fanciers' association`
#ASSERT NOT `the entity meets the charity test` `the members-only tennis club`
#ASSERT NOT `the entity meets the charity test` `the dormant registered charity`
#ASSERT NOT `the entity meets the charity test` `the grandchildren's trust`
#ASSERT NOT `the entity meets the charity test` `the Ministerially directed trust`
#ASSERT NOT `the entity meets the charity test` `the States-governed foundation`
#ASSERT NOT `the entity meets the charity test` `the Guernsey-governed foundation`
#ASSERT NOT `the entity meets the charity test` `the entity with no purposes and no benefit`

-- A10's practical consequence: an entity with NO purposes passes 5(1)(a)
-- vacuously, so on this reading it turns entirely on 5(1)(b). Where the
-- determiner has nonetheless found public benefit, the test is met — which is
-- the reading's uncomfortable edge, recorded rather than hidden.
#ASSERT     `the entity meets the charity test` `the entity with no purposes`
